  "changes": [
    "The actual ordinary-flow tower is selected at fixed directional order k=2, yielding parameterLoss before spatial order zero, component, radius, state or singleton direction. The two optical second-derivative bounds expose this loss explicitly and retain high=loss+parameterLoss.",
    "The zero-offset private equality now transports 0+loss+parameterLoss to loss+parameterLoss by congrArg applied to Nat.zero_add. The genuine optical-travel germ, scalar second derivative, actual tower and right-endpoint curvature-integral limit are otherwise unchanged.",
    "The singleton direction high grade uses loss+parameterLoss, hence its actual material M power is max base(loss+parameterLoss). Both quantitative weight-constraint headers explicitly return the same selected loss. The separate coefficient-tower exponent max base(1+loss) remains unchanged.",
    "The containing-cell cubic exponential proof first receives this fixed order-two loss, then chooses d=max base(1+loss)+2*max base(loss+parameterLoss). The existing true H_M material envelope absorbs that fixed numerical power. No seminorm loss is hidden in an arbitrary constant.",
    "The generic cubic-exponential lemma and both final cubic/index public headers remain byte-identical. The six actual external consumers of control_actual_cell_index_bound therefore retain the same public input/output interface.",
    "All original functions, optical controls, actual C.cell label, any containing D.cells j, H^.75 and E0 sample factors are preserved; no cell identification or new witness is introduced."
  ],
